WEBVTT

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.360
(GROWLS)

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.600
Be still, stranger,
or you'll never move again.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.720
-Who are you?
-I'm Edmund!

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.120
I met the Queen in the woods!
She told me to come back here!

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.960
I'm a Son of Adam!

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.400
My apologies,
fortunate favourite of the queen.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.840
Or else, not so fortunate.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.520
Right this way.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.120
Wait here.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.000
Like it?

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.320
(STAMMERING) Yes, Your Majesty.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.320
I thought you might.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.320
Tell me, Edmund,

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.200
are your sisters deaf?

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.720
No.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:28.040
And your brother, is he

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.520
unintelligent?

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.040
Well, I think so. But Mum says...

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:39.080
Then how dare you come alone!

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.840
-I tried!
-Edmund, I asked so little of you.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.800
-They just don't listen to me!
-You couldn't even do that.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.800
I did bring them halfway.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:50.520
They're at the little house
at the dam with the Beavers.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.800
Well.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.800
I suppose you're not
a total loss then, are you?

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.960
Well, I was wondering,

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:12.640
could I maybe have some more
Turkish delight now?

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.440
Our guest is hungry.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.880
This way for your num-nums.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.360
Maugrim?

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.920
(GROWLING)

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.920
You know what to do.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.560
(HOWLING)

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.560
Hurry, Mother! They're after us!

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.640
-Oh, right then.
-What's she doing?

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.160
Oh, you'll be thanking me later.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.600
It's a long journey and Beaver
gets pretty cranky when he's hungry.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.240
I'm cranky now!

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.160
Take them.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.360
(GROWLING)

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:29.840
-Do you think we'll need jam?
-Only if the Witch serves toast.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.600
(BARKING)

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:46.640
Hurry.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.560
Badger and me dug this.
Comes out right near his place.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.800
You told me it led to your mum's!

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:07.960
(GROANS)

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.200
Lucy!

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.600
(BEAVERS GASP)

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.120
(WHISPERING) They're in the tunnel.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:14.320
-Quick! This way.
-Hurry!

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.880
-Run!
-Quick! Quick! Quick!

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.880
You should have brought a map!

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:31.560
There wasn't room next to the jam.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.720
Come on, Lucy!

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:44.720
(GROANS)

